A||||5||Philphine||finally got wing...and a lesson||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||01-17-2001||12:12 PM||||<BR>back when the "show your wing" thread was going i was whining over the wing that i couldn't get roadway to keep to their schedule and deliver. i finally got it. looked in the box, yep, it's got a wing in it. signed the paper and paid for it. took it out back to see how it would look on the car...and found a pretty good crack in it.<P>it says right on the box inspect before acceptance 'cause once signed for it's yours. i should have looked at it better. i'm pretty sure i can fix it myself with out too much trouble but by all rights i probaly could have returned it.  <P>anyway the wing itself. i like it. if you've got that "riceophobia" thing going it's not for you. the leading edge sits about 14" off the deck and it has louvers in the sides. just like the saleen wing on my '87, the angles and general shape of it make it look like it could have been a fiero wing anyway. i'll have to be careful mounting it though because the holes sit a lot closer to the edges of the trunk. the widest of the 3 (on each side) holes i wont be able to use but i think it will still be sturdy enough. it also has a place for a 3rd brake light i couldn't see in the ad. i'll need to see what fits in it. <P>i was going to put it on my cheap fiero but i'm going to save it for another project i think (cost too much to be part of a cheap thrill project anyway). i promise this time i'll hunt up my camera (need it for a guard trip anyway) and take some pics to snail to some one and they can decide if they want to post them. i'll get some of the wing on my '87 too, plus a few other things i've been trying to describe.  <P>got kind of long. sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||01-17-2001||03:09 PM||||There's nothing wrong with a 2 foot wing...<P><BR>As long as you intend to move te vehicle at speeds which require the extra downforce. Someone posted the #s for the stock wing a while back as per pounds downforce/mph. and it looks like that's plenty, but I guess if you feel the need to go over 150mph and you're looking for that extra little bit of traction so you can hit the nitrous...<P>ok, if you get a fiero to go 150mph, and have more to give... send me an email, I want to see it!||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||01-17-2001||06:29 PM||||Call the company you bought it from before you do anything and tell them what happened. They may take it back for an exchange.||||reg||1
