Z||000004||Coconut||01-17-2001||10:09 PM||||Philphine,<BR>The manufacturer and/or the shipping company involved may have a policy regarding "concealed damage". Anytime we recieve shipped material at our work and sign for it, we are signing based on the condition of the container. If the box that was sent to you was in good shape, well then you are signing for goods that are expected to be in good shape when you open the box. If the wing was cracked, but did not forsee any damage based on the condition of the box, you may have a legitimate claim. I would pursue this course of action. Try calling both companies involved, and explain your situation. It's worth a shot, dude! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Cruisin' <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||4
Z||000005||Philphine||01-18-2001||11:29 AM||||naw...imma keep it. the box itself didn't look too hot. thats why i made sure to look in it. the cracked section was facing the bottom and since it was straped inside the box i did'nt try to take it out.<P>the crack is right on the trailing edge just over the 3rd brake light opening so i can do some repair from the inside. it just seems easier than going through trying to send it back and get another one. i'll just chalk it up to experience.<P>and count, if i haven't found my camera by the time i go on my next trip next month, i may have to take you up on your offer when i get home. it'll be warmer (hopefully) and i can pretend i take better care of it and clean it out. <p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
